    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"A spatial ground-water data base usable in a geographic information system was developed for environmental monitoring in Carson Valley, Nevada and California. The data base includes three thematic data sets: (1) ground-water monitoring sites, (2) ground-water-altitude contours, and (3) depth-to-water contours. The source data is at a scale of 1:62,500 and represents water-table conditions for April and May 1998. Documentation and summary information are included for each spatial data set. Software to access and perform basic geographic operations on the data sets also is included.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
